tk-drm-upstream: Linux DRM core type definitions and ports (x86_64, v7.2.3)
==========================================================================

Layer: platform. Depends only on tk-linux-kapi (kernel-API shims).

Type modules (`*_types.rs`) mirror Linux 7.2.3 definitions named in their
headers. Their layouts were generated from DWARF of the configured Linux
oracle (`config/linux/7.2.3-q35-graphics.config`, THP enabled), and every size
and field offset is pinned by a compile-time assertion. DWARF generation does
not itself establish a license: source-header identifiers and permissions are
file-specific. In particular, the new sysfb/screen-info types below come from
GPL-2.0 headers; they are not described here as MIT-licensed.

Function ports (`*_upstream.rs`) mirror the Linux `.c` files named in their
header comments. Each stub is filled by its owning batch (see the module
header comment).

Linux sources are licensed per file. The following list records the source
identifiers as found in the local Linux 7.2.3 tree; an MIT `SPDX` line in a Rust
translation does not change the identifier of a GPL-only source it follows.
The source-license identifiers called out below are reflected by each Rust
translation's SPDX marker, except where the named source offers a separate MIT
option selected by that translation:

