GPL text: `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt` and `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt` are
verbatim copies of Linux 7.2.3 `LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0`, including its
license-identifier metadata and complete GPL version 2 text. The latter file
records the upstream or-later grant; it does not remove that grant's scope.
`Cargo.toml` declares the package mix as `MIT AND GPL-2.0-only AND
GPL-2.0-or-later`. The `// upstream:` comments identify source correspondences;
per-file mapping is also listed in the 2026-10-16 migration section of
`docs/upstream-provenance.md`.

Test fixtures: every EDID used by the host tests is built in code
(`drm_edid_upstream.rs`, `tests` module). No Linux test data is copied.

Pending-stub definitions (`src/pending_stubs/`) are temporary, owned by later
batches, and each names its replacing Linux file in its module header.
